{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788178825914750204,"compiled_state":{"alias":"nauseating-inquiring-ibex","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"dc021e2cb3707f1f80a921f0415bb12f85c8397e42780396a618e4d3b606fb8f","event_uuid":"aedcaee6-6869-4372-8511-dd5ed94fd9fc","position":{"commit_sha":"ecd0ed96443ca220689e0d225a675e1d2cf59fac","position":"1788158688930308001-aedcaee6-6869-4372-8511-dd5ed94fd9fc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"14b1dd8169ffbad3fe2575f019b60bca2b28ffa0ca973fff337cabcd76cb4789","event_uuid":"b63a8858-e9e5-4c3b-8c13-25831e0f14a3","position":{"commit_sha":"9164062044a58f8016dc2d55f8536d74dd69f92b","position":"1788158712985563001-b63a8858-e9e5-4c3b-8c13-25831e0f14a3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788158688930308001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[],"description":"Reduce rebar tickets-store growth and reclaim the ~1 GiB already spent, by making the\nreconciler's committed `.bridge_state` cache cheap instead of re-homing it.\n\nMeasured facts, full research trail and the three corrected false premises: session_log\n**1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (dinky-frowsy-woodborer). Supersedes the tabled plan in\n**bronze-used-foxhound** (e594-e1d0). Umbrella: **1270-b740**.\n\n## Context\n\nThe `tickets` branch is **1.04 GiB**; **92%** is the reconciler's `.bridge_state` cache, not\nticket data (events are 55 MB). Diffing consecutive committed revisions of `bindings.json`\n(1509 bindings) shows the growth is bookkeeping nothing reads:\n\n| field | entries changed per pass |\n|---|---|\n| `baseline` (the value) | **0** |\n| `baseline_advanced_at` (written at `binding_store.py:375`, read nowhere in `src/`) | **1144** |\n| `last_get_pass` (rotation bookkeeping) | **20** |\n\nA scattered edit across a sort-ordered 18 MB file defeats git delta compression. Measured on 40\nconsecutive real revisions rebuilt in a clean repo and repacked `--window=250 --depth=50`, true\nmarginal cost per version is **12.79 KB** today, **1.74 KB** after deleting the timestamp (7.4x),\nand the version count halves once rotation bookkeeping moves out (12.8x total).\n\n## Approach and why this one\n\nKeep the cache committed and make it cheap. `.bridge_state` must stay on-branch because the\nreconciler runs on **ephemeral** GitHub-hosted runners, so durable state has to live in git — an\nearlier design wrote prev to the main-branch worktree, so prev was always `{}` and the differ\nre-derived 2050+ inbound creates every pass (`reconcile.py:258-259`). Epic `6c9c` evaluated and\ndropped re-homing it off-branch (WS-1) because the convergence loop already self-heals binding\ndrift. So the levers are content and churn, not location.\n\nThe one-time reclaim of existing history is included (child A6) under an operator-approved\nquiescence protocol. Its mechanics are **proven, not theoretical**: `git fast-export --no-data |\nfilter | git fast-import` on the real branch produced 1,172,586,762 -> 98,803,422 bytes (8.4%)\nwith all 49,888 commits and 2,661 merges preserved and the HEAD tree byte-identical except the\nintended paths. Stock git plumbing only — `git-filter-repo` is deliberately **not** used: it is an\nunwanted core dependency and it prunes empty commits, which would reshape the DAG that\nancestry-based authorship verification walks.\n\n## Scope (children, in dependency order)\n\n1. **A1** delete `baseline_advanced_at` + write-when-changed guard in `set_baseline`\n2. **A2-1** move `last_get_pass` to `.bridge_state/get_rotation.json`; read `max(new, legacy)`\n3. **A3** text-normalize baseline description/status/priority (exclude `assignee`)\n4. **A2-2** delete the legacy in-line `last_get_pass` field (gated on writer rollout)\n5. **A4-1/2/3** `bridge_fsck` fence, then `prev_snapshot` -> key-set, then branch-3 empty-payload skip\n6. **A5** ADR covering all three committed-format changes\n7. **A6** one-time reclaim under the quiescence protocol (LAST; requires A1-A5 and Epic B's B6)\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nThree committed-format changes to a shared store file, each with a stated boundary. A2-1 is\nreversible (it never stops writing the legacy field). A3 is reversible because the read path\ncanonicalizes both shapes idempotently. A2-2 and A4-2 are the irreversible steps: A2-2 is gated on\nobserved writer rollout; reverting A4-2 requires the reverse-direction corpus diff recorded first.\nA6 is gated on an off-repo backup bundle plus a fail-closed epoch guard, and its resumability is\nexplicitly **none** — mitigated by running every correctness assertion on a scratch clone before\nanything is published.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Marginal packed cost per changed `bindings.json` version is **<=25% of the pre-change\n      baseline measured by the same method** (rebuild N>=40 consecutive revisions in a clean repo,\n      repack `--window=250 --depth=50`, compute `(pack_N - pack_1)/(N-1)`). Baseline today 12.79 KB.\n      Verify: the measurement script recorded in the child ticket.\n- [ ] Two consecutive reconciler passes over unchanged Jira state produce a **byte-identical**\n      `bindings.json` and create **no commit**. Tier: integration against a stateful fake asserting\n      file bytes and commit count, not call counts.\n- [ ] `baseline_advanced_at` is absent from every entry written by `set_baseline`, and no `src/`\n      reference to it remains. Verify: `grep -r baseline_advanced_at src/` returns nothing.\n- [ ] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store leaves the worktree byte-identical\n      (`git status --porcelain` empty) — the read-only path must not persist a migration.\n- [ ] A **dict-shaped** baseline fed through the live `compute_update_fields` path yields the same\n      verdict as its normalized-string equivalent. This test does not exist today; the existing\n      cells use flat strings only, so a no-op-on-strings normalizer would pass while proving\n      nothing. Tier: integration through the real production comparison path.\n- [ ] Corpus mutation-diff (full prev vs key-set prev) over >=4 real snapshot pairs shows zero\n      difference in any mutation reaching Jira with a non-empty effect, **and** the reverse-direction\n      diff is recorded as the A4-2 rollback artifact.\n- [ ] `outbound_differ.py` is **<=800 LOC** after the rotation extraction (it is at exactly 800\n      today; the locked module-size gate fails the build on 801).\n- [ ] A fresh **unfiltered** clone of `tickets` is **<=150 MB**, `HEAD^{tree}` equals the recorded\n      pre-rewrite tip tree, and commit and merge-commit counts are unchanged (measured at window\n      time, not hardcoded).\n- [ ] After the review bot's first post-window write, `git merge-base --is-ancestor <old-tip>\n      origin/tickets` is **false** (the assertion that actually proves non-resurrection) and\n      `size-pack` growth is <1 MB.\n- [ ] A clone on a stale epoch attempting to push **aborts and performs no merge** at **both**\n      guarded sites (`sync._union_merge` and `push.py`'s non-FF retry). Tier: integration in two\n      real temporary clones with divergent epochs.\n- [ ] An ADR exists enumerating all three committed-format changes, the mixed-version protocol, the\n      A2-2 gate, and each rollback boundary.\n- [ ] The off-repo backup bundle exists and `git bundle verify` passes. **[operator-attested]**\n- [ ] Operator has confirmed zero active sessions and all `rebar-mcp` servers stopped before the\n      reclaim window. **[operator-attested]**","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"baseline guard + rotation extraction + normalization"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"_advance_baselines caller; prev persist"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py","reason":"branch-3 empty-payload skip"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/sync.py","reason":"epoch guard at _union_merge"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push.py","reason":"epoch guard before its own merges"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"epoch field + remote-side reader"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"95da-0b4f-06a8-4b9c","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Bound tickets-store growth: make the committed .bridge_state cache cheap + one-time reclaim of the spent ~1 GiB","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["aedcaee6-6869-4372-8511-dd5ed94fd9fc","b63a8858-e9e5-4c3b-8c13-25831e0f14a3"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788178825914750204,"uuid":"696e50d2-5ce1-45e1-b08f-729e74655403"}